/**
 * @typedef {Object} InitiatePaymentFlowArgs
 * @property {string} [external_id] - Your unique reference for this payment, such as an order or invoice number. You can use this ID later to look up the payment instead of our payment ID. Must be unique within this merchant account's payments. 1–128 characters after trimming leading and trailing whitespace. Must start with a letter or digit. Remaining characters may be letters, digits, periods (`.`), underscores (`_`), colons (`:`), slashes (`/`), or hyphens (`-`). Blank or whitespace-only values are stored as null.
 * @property {string} amount - The payment amount in the smallest currency unit (e.g. satang). For example, use 10000 for 100 THB. Must be a positive integer.
 * @property {string} currency - The three-letter ISO currency code (e.g. THB). Must match the currency configured for your merchant account.
 * @property {string} payment_session_id - The session ID received from our SDK after the customer selects their payment method. This connects the customer's payment method choice to this payment.
 * @property {string} [card_id] - The ID of a previously saved card (starting with `crd_`) or your own external card identifier. When provided for a card payment session that doesn't have a token attached, we'll use this saved card's token for the payment.  Required when the payment session's payment method is CARD and no token was provided during select-payment-method.
 * @property {boolean} capture - Controls when funds are captured. Set to true to capture funds immediately upon payment authorization, or false to only authorize funds for later capture. Useful for businesses that ship physical goods or need to verify orders before charging.
 * @property {string} return_url - The URL where we'll redirect your customer after they complete the payment flow. Should be a page that can handle both successful and failed payments.
 * @property {string} [customer_id] - Either a Customer ID (starting with `ctc_`) or your own external customer identifier. We'll link this payment to an existing customer if found, or create a new customer if not. This helps track payment history per customer.  If you provide your own external ID and a customer with that ID doesn't exist, we'll create a new customer using that ID as their external identifier.
 * @property {string} [customer_email] - The customer's email address. If provided, we'll either:  - Link this payment to an existing customer with this email - Create a new customer with this email if no match is found - Update the email for the customer specified in customer_id (if provided)
 * @property {string} [customer_mobile] - The customer's mobile number. If provided, we'll either:  - Link this payment to an existing customer with this mobile - Create a new customer with this mobile if no match is found - Update the mobile for the customer specified in customer_id (if provided)
 * @property {string} [customer_name] - The customer's name. If provided, we'll either:  - Update the name for an existing customer if found - Set the name when creating a new customer - Update the name for the customer specified in customer_id (if provided)
 * @property {string} [save_card] - Option to save the card used in this payment session to the contact. Only applicable when the payment session uses a card token. The card will be saved if the token is multi-use.  - `ADD`: Add the card to the contact without setting it as default - `DEFAULT`: Add the card to the contact and set it as the default card  If any error occurs while saving the card, it will be silently ignored and will not block the payment flow.
 * @property {("customer"|"merchant")} [interest_bearer] - Assertion that the payment session was locked to this interest bearer: `customer` or `merchant`. The interest bearer is fixed when the customer picks their plan in `select-payment-method`, and this only confirms it.  Required when the payment session's payment method is INSTALLMENT, and it must be the same value that applied to `select-payment-method` for this session, otherwise the request is rejected.
 */

